<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Itza people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Itza Maya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Itza are a Maya people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> lakes in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>. Their traditions trace them to Chichen Itza in Yucatán, after whose decline they moved south and founded the kingdom of Nojpetén. They remained independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> until 1697, the last Maya kingdom to fall, and a few speakers of their language survive around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-peten-itza">Lake Petén Itzá</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/itza-people.jpg" alt="Itza people" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Castillo,_Chich%C3%A9n_Itz%C3%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
